            <ArticleTitle>Neurectomy for Bilateral Morton's Neuroma A Case Report of a Male Patient.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>229-34</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.7547/14-161</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Morton's neuroma is a common condition that mainly affects middle-aged women, and many articles have addressed the surgical treatment of this condition. Previous reports have described bilateral neuroma excision in women but not in men. We report a rare case of bilateral neuromas in a male patient treated with simultaneous neurectomy.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
